<h2><a href="#linux"  >Programming</a> - Debugging</h2></p>
The Nine Indispensable Rules for Finding Even the Most Elusive Software
and Hardware Problems</p>

UNDERSTAND THE SYSTEM</br>
There's a side benefit to understanding your own systems, too. When you do find the bugs, you'll
need to fix them without breaking anything else. Understanding what the system is supposed to do
is the first step toward not breaking it.</p>
MAKE IT FAIL</br>

QUIT THINKING AND LOOK</br>

DIVIDE AND CONQUER</br>

CHANGE ONE THING AT A TIME</br>

KEEP AN AUDIT TRAIL</br>

CHECK THE PLUG</br>

GET A FRESH VIEW</br>

IF YOU DIDN'T FIX IT, IT AIN'T FIXED</br>

